From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:12:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] hw/arm: Add the Chumby Classic machine

The Chumby Classic: an i.MX21 with 64 MiB of SDRAM, 64 MiB of NAND flash
(-drive if=mtd), a 320x240 LCD with a TSC2100 touchscreen on CSPI3 and
its pen interrupt on GPIO PE19, and the crypto processor on UART3.

It boots a zImage directly as an MX21ADS (machine type 851), the type
the Chumby's own kernel is built for, with the stock command line unless
-append is given. The device's own 2.6.16 kernel and root disk run
unmodified to its control panel.

Signed-off-by: John Merchant <john@johnmerchant.dev>
