+++ b/docs/system/arm/chumby-classic.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,63 @@
+Chumby Classic (``chumby-classic``)
+===================================
+
+The ``chumby-classic`` machine emulates the Chumby Classic, a Wi-Fi
+internet appliance with a 320x240 touchscreen built around the Freescale
+i.MX21 SoC (ARM926EJ-S). It runs the device's own Linux 2.6.16 kernel and
+root disk unmodified, booting them from an image of its NAND flash.
+
+Emulated devices:
+
+- ARM926EJ-S CPU and 64 MiB of SDRAM
+- AITC interrupt controller
+- GPT1-3 timers
+- UART1-4 (UART1 is the console)
+- The crypto processor on UART3, with a made-up identity (hardware
+  version 3.8, GUID ``C40BB1E0-0000-4000-8000-0E4000000001``, serial
+  number ``0000000000000000``); it holds no keys and refuses key and
+  challenge requests
+- Clock and reset module, PLLs locked at the boot loader's settings
+- GPIO ports A-F
+- CSPI1-3, with a TI TSC2100 touchscreen controller on CSPI3
+- LCD controller: background plane and graphic window, 16 bpp
+- NAND flash controller with a 64 MiB small-page NAND chip
+- PWM, and the USB host's root hub (no devices)
+
+Missing devices:
+
+- DMA, SSI audio, keypad, watchdog, RTC, SDHC, I2C and the USB transfer
+  engine: their registers read back what was last written
+
+Boot options
+------------
+
+The machine boots a Linux kernel directly, as the Chumby's boot loader
+does: ``-kernel`` takes a zImage, which is entered with machine type 851
+(MX21ADS), the type the Chumby's kernel is built for. Without
+``-append``, the kernel gets the stock command line for the first root
+disk::
+
+  console=ttyS0,38400 root=/dev/mtdblock5 rootfstype=cramfs init=/linuxrc chumby_hwversion=3.8
+
+The NAND flash is a raw image given with ``-drive if=mtd``. Its layout is
+that of ``nanddump``: 131072 records of 528 bytes, each a page's 512 data
+bytes followed by its 16 spare bytes, 69206016 bytes in all. Programs and
+erases are written back to the image unless the drive is read-only or a
+snapshot.
+
+Running
+-------
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+  $ qemu-system-arm -M chumby-classic -kernel zImage \
+      -drive if=mtd,file=nand.img,format=raw -serial stdio
+
+The pen is the absolute pointer: the left button presses the screen. It
+can also be driven from QMP with ``input-send-event`` (``abs`` events on
+the ``x`` and ``y`` axes, 0 to 32767 across the screen, and the ``left``
+button). ``screendump`` captures the screen.
+
+The emulated clock follows the host's. ``-icount shift=auto,sleep=off``
+lets it run ahead while the guest is idle, which boots several times
+faster.
